    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Drikke dus»",
     "texto": [
      "«Drikke dus» is the toast and drink you have after agreeing to say «du» to each other; traditionally it was done with arms linked. In everyday Danish today, **du** is the neutral form of address and **De** is formal and rare. The choice depends on the situation and the preferences of the speakers, not only on age."
     ],
     "tutora": "contenta"
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "With an adjective, there is an article",
     "texto": [
      "Without an adjective, the profession has **no article**, unlike English («a teacher»): Han er **lærer**. Hun er **muslim**.\n\nBut with an adjective, the article comes back: Han var **en dansk** filosof."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    }
   ]
